            <ArticleTitle>Use of vacuum assisted closure therapy in the palliation of a malignant wound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>477-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Vaccum assisted closure (VAC) therapy is a novel method of wound healing using topical negative pressure across the wound bed and containing all exudate within a sealed system. We report the use of VAC therapy to control pain and exudate of a malignant wound.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
